  "_note": "Crash sounds (audio/crash.js plays them; npm run sounds makes the files from synth). impacts: for each sound family, three takes each of a tap, a crunch and a crash (garage/damage.js says which, by strength: data/damage.json classes); materials: which family each thing the car can hit sounds like (physics/impacts.js material, or a collider's own sound: a building, a tree, a tyre wall, a rail). A hit plays one of its takes at random, a little higher or lower (pitch: ± share) and louder the harder it was within its class (gain: [at its weakest, at its hardest] for each class). scrape: a loop for sliding along metal or anything else, its level following the scrape (gain at full) and its pitch the speed. glass, light: a window or a light breaking. tear: a part tearing off. clatter: a torn-off part bouncing (light and heavy takes; gain [at clatterFrom, hardest]). rattle: a loop for loose parts rattling, its level following how much. flap: a hanging panel flapping in the wind. heavy: the low thump under a big crash.",
